# death_if_fails rescaled for real per-act risk (drafts/repeats/rescale_death.py)
# Chroma library, modern Earth: ADULT LOVE, DESIRE AND INTIMACY (next batch, Emren's point 11: "have threesome sex
# somehow... There are lots of things that character can interact. We need to create a world of possibilities with
# color philosophy framework"). Brief: drafts/next2/BRIEF.md. Rules: library-spec.md. Syntax: header of build.py.
# Adults only (18 and over). Everything is consensual between adults and fades to black: labels say the choice,
# scenes and outcome lines carry the before and the morning after, never sexual detail.
# Layout: ten everyday moments whose calls cover the ten color pairs once, arranged so each group the engine shows is
# color-even in its calls: the five for people without a partner call each color twice, and so do the five with a
# partner; the five open to young adults call each color twice, and so do the five open to elders; adults and
# mature people meet all ten. Cross cycles s1 s1 s1 s2 s2 s2 s3 s3 s4 s4.
# Two life events take the two halves of line D1 (pairs), so all ten pairs appear once.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- without a partner: calls RG (cycle s2)

# gate: age >= 18
== someone asks you home after the party
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-50
calls: RG
excludes: partner
tone: joy
life: love, friends
horizon: moment
roles: prospect, friend
earth: two in the morning at a friend's party, and someone you met tonight asks if you want to go back to theirs
times: Many young adults, a few times in their twenties and less after; 60 to 80 in 100 North American students have had some hookup (Garcia and colleagues 2012 review)
gap: 3-6
scene: It is nearly two in the morning, the party is thinning out, and {prospect}, whom {N} met by the kitchen sink four hours ago, asks quietly whether {N} wants to go back to theirs.
scene W: {N} came with {friend} and promised to share the taxi home. {prospect} is lovely, and a promise is still a promise.
scene U: {N} has spent the whole evening finding things out about {prospect}: the strange job, the scar on one wrist, the laugh. There is so much more to know.
scene B: {N} wanted {prospect} from the moment they walked in, and has spent the evening making sure the feeling was returned. It was.
scene R: The music is still going, {Ns} heart is going faster, and {prospect} has hold of {Ns} hand by the pile of coats.
scene G: There is something easy between {N} and {prospect}, as if they have known each other for years, and the air outside smells of rain.
- W | say goodnight at the door, swap numbers, and ask them to dinner next week | v: conformity, security | chance: 85
- U | sit on the stairs asking them questions till three, and decide nothing tonight | v: self-direction | self_control: + | chance: 90
- B | go home with them, and slip out before breakfast without leaving a number | v: hedonism, power | chance: 80
- R | go home with them, laughing, and leave your coat behind | habit | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 85
- G | walk them home through the rain, and let the night decide the rest | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 75
- W>B | say you never go home with anyone on a first night, and let them chase | v: power, conformity | chance: 75
- U>R | take the pill they offer first, after looking it up on your phone | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: used drugs | closed: law: an illegal drug; backfire: a frightening night in hospital | death_if_fails: 0.002 | law: drugs | chance: 70
- B>G | bring them back to your own place, where you know the door and the street | v: security, hedonism | chance: 80
- R>W | find the friend you came with, say where you are going, and then go | v: benevolence, hedonism | chance: 75
- G>U | go back with them and talk till dawn, to see who they are by daylight | v: self-direction, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 85
works: {N} wakes up happy, with a new number in the phone and nothing to regret.
works: The night ends the way {N} hoped, and the walk home at dawn feels like flying.
fails: The morning after is awkward, and the bus home takes forever.
fails: {N} never hears from {prospect} again, and the friends from the party have plenty to say.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- without a partner: calls UR (cycle s1)

# gate: age >= 18; back to dating after a long relationship or years alone (ago_end_partner >= 1, or never partnered by thirty)
== a match who wants to meet tonight
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 28-80
calls: UR
excludes: partner
tone: mixed
life: love
horizon: moment
roles: prospect, friend
earth: back on the dating apps after years, and a match who seems lovely wants you to come over tonight
times: Many people back on the apps after years, several times in a dating stretch; Pew 2023: 3 in 10 US adults have ever used a dating site or app
gap: 2-4
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: {N} is back on the apps after years away, and {prospect}, a few messages in, asks whether {N} would like to come over tonight.
scene W: {N} was raised to meet people properly: in daylight, with a name, and a friend who knows where. Tonight is not how things are done.
scene U: {N} has read everything about how the apps work now, and still cannot tell from six photographs who {prospect} really is.
scene B: For years {N} did what other people wanted. Tonight {N} can have exactly what {N} wants, and the phone keeps buzzing.
scene R: The messages are funny, the photos are lovely, and {N} has not felt this awake in a long time.
scene G: {N} reads the messages three times over, listening for the person behind them, the way one listens for weather.
- W | say not tonight, and ask to meet for coffee in daylight on Saturday | v: security, conformity | chance: 80
- U | ask for a short video call first, to see who is really there | v: security, self-direction | tech: video calls | chance: 80
- B | say yes, but at a bar of your choosing, and leave whenever you like | v: power, security | chance: 85
- R | say yes, shower, and be at their door within the hour | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 70
- G | read their messages once more, and go only if your gut says yes | v: self-direction, security | chance: 80
- W>U | keep messaging for a week, the old-fashioned way, to learn who they are | v: security, self-direction | chance: 70
- U>B | ask a few careful questions to test their story, and go only if it holds | v: security, power | chance: 70
- B>R | knock five years off your age, and say yes to tonight | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 65
- R>G | admit you are out of practice and nervous, and see what they say | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 80
- G>W | ask around among friends you share, as people used to, before saying yes | v: security, tradition | chance: 70
works: The evening is easy and warm, and {N} feels like {N} again.
works: {prospect} turns out to be just as kind as the messages, and a second date is set before the night is over.
fails: {prospect} looks nothing like the photographs, and {N} is home by ten.
fails: The evening goes flat after the first hour, and {N} deletes the app on the bus home.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- without a partner: calls BG (cycle s3)

# gate: age >= 18; a partnership ended within the last three years (ago_end_partner <= 3), and the ex is single
== your ex wants to try again
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 19-55
calls: BG
excludes: partner
tone: mixed
life: love
horizon: week
roles: prospect, friend, sibling
earth: months after the breakup, your ex calls late one evening and asks if the two of you could try again
times: Many people after a breakup, once or twice in a life; nearly half of US young adults in one study had got back together with an ex (Halpern-Meekin and colleagues 2013)
gap: 3-6
scene: Eight months after the breakup, {prospect} calls late on a Sunday and asks, in a small voice, whether the two of them could try again.
scene W: At the end {N} said it was over for good, and meant it. {N} is not someone who says such things lightly.
scene U: {N} has spent eight months working out what went wrong. Now the question is whether any of it can be put right.
scene B: Last time {N} was the one who got hurt. This time {N} holds the cards, and both of them know it.
scene R: The sound of that voice on the phone goes straight to the stomach, the way it always did.
scene G: Some things come round again like the seasons. The old jumper is still in {Ns} drawer, and it still smells faintly of {prospect}.
- W | say no, kindly and firmly, as you said at the end | v: conformity, security | mark: kept your word | chance: 80
- U | meet for coffee and go through, honestly, what broke last time | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | say maybe, and let them work hard to win you back | v: power | act: say maybe, and let the ex work hard to win them back | chance: 70
- R | tell them to come round tonight, and stop thinking | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 65
- G | get back together, and slip back into the old Sunday mornings | binds | v: security, tradition | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | chance: 60
- W>R | agree to one date with rules: no staying over, no talking about the past | v: hedonism, conformity | chance: 50
- U>G | write down what each of you would have to change, and try for three months | binds | v: benevolence, self-direction | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | chance: 60
- B>W | agree to try again if they apologise properly, in front of your friends | v: power (face), conformity | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | chance: 60
- R>U | spend one more night together, to find out whether anything is still there | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 65
- G>B | take them back for the comfort, and keep an eye out for someone better | v: security, power | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 70
works: {N} and {prospect} talk until the old hurt loses its sharp edge, and whatever they decide feels right.
works: The second try starts slowly and honestly, and {N} likes who they both are now.
fails: Within a month the old fights are back, word for word.
fails: {N} ends up hurt again, and {Ns} friends try hard not to say they saw it coming.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- without a partner: calls WU (cycle s4)

# gate: age >= 18; the friend is of a sex the character is drawn to (the game draws {friend} so)
== a friend says they are in love with you
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-60
calls: WU
excludes: partner
tone: mixed
life: love, friends
horizon: week
roles: friend
earth: over the washing-up after dinner, a close friend of years admits they have been in love with you for a long time
times: Perhaps 1 in 3 adults, once or twice (estimate); about two thirds of the couples in one study began as friends (Stinson and colleagues 2021)
gap: 6-12
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
share: .33
scene: Over the washing-up after dinner, {friend} puts down the tea towel and says it plainly: they have been in love with {N} for years.
scene W: {N} and {friend} have been there for each other through everything. Whatever {N} says next, {N} will not be careless with it.
scene U: {N} replays ten years of small moments in a few seconds, and suddenly every one of them means something different.
scene B: Someone has wanted {N} for years without a word, and {N} finds the thought is far from unpleasant.
scene R: {Ns} face goes hot. {friend} is standing very close, waiting, and the kitchen tap is still running.
scene G: Ten years of shared dinners, shared holidays, a dog walked together on Sundays. Perhaps this was always what was growing.
- W | tell them gently that you love them as a friend, and that nothing changes | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 75
- U | ask for a week, and spend it working out honestly what you feel | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- B | let them keep hoping; being adored is pleasant, and it is free | v: power, hedonism | chance: 70
- R | kiss them, there in the kitchen, with the tap still running | v: stimulation, hedonism | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | chance: 70
- G | let it grow slowly, and see whether the friendship turns into more | v: benevolence | self_control: + | chance: 65
- W>G | say yes, and tell both your families together at the next birthday | identity | v: tradition, benevolence | title: girlfriend or boyfriend | chance: 65
- U>W | talk through, carefully, what a romance would risk for the friendship | v: benevolence, security | chance: 60
- B>U | tell a friend you share, in confidence, to find out who else knew | v: self-direction, security | chance: 70
- R>B | say yes tonight, because it feels good to be wanted, and think later | v: hedonism, power (face) | chance: 70
- G>R | walk out with them under the stars, and say whatever comes | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 75
works: Whatever {N} answers, the two of them are still laughing together a month later.
works: The friendship bends without breaking, and something new grows out of it.
fails: Things go stiff and careful between them, and the dinners stop.
fails: {friend} pulls away for a long while, and {N} misses them more than expected.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- without a partner: calls WB (cycle s1)

# gate: age >= 30; ~held_partner for five years or more, by choice (no breakup in the last two years: ago_end_partner >= 2, or never partnered)
== single by choice, and everyone asks why
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-80
calls: WB
excludes: partner
tone: mixed
life: love, family
horizon: moment
roles: parent, sibling, friend, a cousin
earth: at a cousin's wedding, the third relative of the evening asks when you will find someone, and you are happily single
times: Most adults single by choice, at many family gatherings, less as the years pass; Pew 2020: half of single US adults are not looking for a relationship or dates
gap: 2-4
scene: At a cousin's wedding, {parent} leans over the dessert and asks, for the third time this year, whether {N} has met anyone nice.
scene W: Everyone at the table is seated in couples, the way the plan said. {N} has been put at the end, next to a great-aunt.
scene U: {N} has thought hard about this for years and knows exactly why a life alone suits. Explaining it over wedding cake is another matter.
scene B: {N} has a flat, money and evenings that belong to nobody else, and has no plan to hand any of them over.
scene R: {N} loves this life: the late trips, the nights out, the freedom to say yes to anything at all. The questions sting anyway.
scene G: {N} has made a full life out of friends, a garden, nieces and nephews. Not every tree needs another tree beside it.
- W | agree to meet the friend of a friend they keep mentioning, to keep the peace | v: conformity | mark: gave in to pressure | self_control: - | chance: 80
- U | explain, calmly and clearly, why you have chosen a life on your own | identity | v: self-direction | chance: 65
- B | tell them, in front of the whole table, that your private life is your own business | identity | v: power, self-direction | mark: made an enemy | chance: 75
- R | laugh, pull the nearest stranger onto the floor, and dance | body: light | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 85
- G | let it wash over you; the family asks out of love | v: benevolence, tradition | act: let it wash over them, since the family asks out of love | chance: 75
- W>U | promise your parent one honest talk about it after the wedding, and really listen | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 70
- U>B | keep a few clever replies ready, and win every exchange | v: power (face) | chance: 85
- B>R | answer with your latest trip and promotion, until they envy your freedom | v: power (face), hedonism | chance: 75
- R>G | raise a glass to everyone at the wedding who came alone, and to friendship | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 65
- G>W | spend the evening with the children and the old aunts, being the one who helps | identity | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 75
works: The questions stop, or stop mattering, and {N} dances until the band packs up.
works: {parent} hears {N} out, and for the first time seems to understand.
fails: The evening turns into a long, kind interrogation, and {N} leaves early.
fails: Long after the wedding, {N} lies awake wondering whether everyone else knows something {N} does not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- with a partner: calls UB (cycle s2)

# gate: age >= 18
== your partner asks to open the relationship
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 20-60
calls: UB
needs: partner
tone: mixed
life: love, home
horizon: months
roles: partner, friend
earth: one night your partner says they love you and want to stay, and would like you both to be free to see other people
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 10 adults ever meet it (share .1), once with each partner they have between 20 and 60, so two or three times in all for most who meet it (estimate; needs: partner makes once: yes once per partner); about 1 in 5 US single adults have ever been in an open relationship (Haupert and colleagues 2017)
once: yes
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
share: .1
scene: After dinner {partner} takes a long breath and says it: they love {N}, they want to stay, and they would like the two of them to be free to see other people.
scene W: {N} and {partner} made promises to each other, and {N} has kept every one of them. Now {partner} wants to rewrite them.
scene U: {partner} has clearly been reading about this for months. {N} wants to know everything: why, who, how it would work, what it would mean.
scene B: {N} hears the question and thinks at once of the neighbour who has been smiling for weeks. Freedom, after all, works both ways.
scene R: Something flares in {Ns} chest, hurt or anger or a strange excitement, and {N} cannot tell which.
scene G: {N} looks round the kitchen they painted together, at the plant on the sill that has come with them through three homes, and wonders what a couple is meant to be.
- W | say no: you promised each other one person, and that promise stands | v: conformity, tradition | mark: kept your word | chance: 60
- U | read about it together, and talk for weeks before deciding anything | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | say yes, and line up someone of your own before they do | v: power, hedonism | chance: 65
- R | tell them, shaking, that they can leave tonight if that is what they want | v: none clear (hurt) | chance: 50
- G | ask what is missing between the two of you, and tend to that first | v: benevolence, security | chance: 60
- W>B | agree to try an open relationship for a while, with written rules you set | binds | v: power, security | chance: 60
- U>R | say yes out of curiosity, and see what you learn about yourself | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 50
- B>G | say yes, then quietly make sure they never have the time or the chance | v: security | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 55
- R>W | say how hurt and scared you are, and ask to stay just the two of you | v: benevolence, security | chance: 70
- G>U | take a weekend away, just the two of you, and let the real reason come out | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 60
works: The long talk goes deep, and {N} and {partner} come out of it closer than they went in.
works: Whatever they decide, they decide it together, and it holds.
fails: The question sits between them for months, and every late message becomes a suspicion.
fails: {partner} is wounded by the answer, and the house goes quiet in a new way.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- with a partner: calls WR (cycle s3)

# gate: age >= 18; holds a job (holds: kind:career below)
== the last night of a work trip
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 22-64
calls: WR
needs: partner
holds: kind:career
tone: trouble
life: love, work
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, partner
earth: the last night of a conference in another city, and at the lift the colleague you have grown close to asks if you want to come up
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 6 working adults, once or twice (estimate); about 1 in 3 US workers have had a romance with a colleague (SHRM 2022)
gap: 6-12
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
share: .17
scene: It is the last night of the conference. At the hotel lift {colleague}, whom {N} has laughed with all week, holds the door and asks quietly whether {N} wants to come up.
scene W: {N} made a promise to {partner}, who is at home tonight putting out the bins. The promise is {Ns} to keep, here as much as there.
scene U: {N} has noticed everything this week: the glances, the excuses to sit together. {N} knows exactly what is being asked, and wonders what it says about home.
scene B: Nobody here knows {partner}. Nobody at home knows this hotel. {N} sees the shape of the chance very clearly.
scene R: Three days of laughing, two glasses of wine, and {colleague} is holding the lift door with a look that turns {Ns} knees to water.
scene G: {N} thinks of the kitchen at home, the dog asleep on the sofa beside {partner}, the smell of that particular house, and feels the pull of both.
- W | say goodnight, and drive home through the night as you promised your partner | v: conformity, benevolence | mark: kept your word | death_if_fails: 0.002 | tech: car | chance: 85
- U | go up for one drink and an honest talk, and nothing more | v: self-direction | chance: 55
- B | go up, and tell yourself that what happens away from home stays away | v: hedonism, power | mark: broke your word | closed: approval: betraying your partner; backfire: found out, and the trust gone | self_control: - | chance: 55
- R | kiss them once against the lift door, and then walk away | v: stimulation | chance: 60
- G | go back to your own room and fall asleep thinking of home | v: security, tradition | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 85
- W>R | go up with them, and confess it all to your partner the day you get home | v: hedonism, benevolence | mark: broke your word | closed: approval: betraying your partner; backfire: the confession ends it | chance: 50
- U>G | turn them down, and plan on the train home how to win back your partner | v: benevolence | mark: kept your word | chance: 80
- B>W | pay whatever it costs for a seat on the last flight home tonight | v: security, conformity | self_control: + | tech: plane | chance: 80
- R>U | stay in the bar with them till closing, talking about everything, then go up alone | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 75
- G>B | go up with them, and keep it from your partner to protect the home you have | v: hedonism, security | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: deceiving your partner; backfire: found out, and the home in pieces | self_control: - | chance: 50
works: The trip ends without harm at home, and {N} walks in the door glad to be back.
works: Whatever happened at the lift, {N} goes home clear about what {N} wants.
fails: {colleague} is cold and strange at work for months afterwards.
fails: {partner} senses something the moment {N} walks in, and asks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- with a partner: calls WG (cycle s4)

# gate: age >= 30; yrs_partner >= 5
== years together, and the bedroom has gone quiet
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-85
calls: WG
needs: partner
tone: trouble
life: love, home
horizon: months
roles: partner, friend
earth: years together, and it has been months since you and your partner last made love; neither of you mentions it
times: Most long-term couples at some point, often more than once (estimate); in the US General Social Survey sex grows less frequent with age and years together
gap: 4-8
scene: It has been months since {N} and {partner} last made love. Neither of them says so. They kiss goodnight, put out the lamp and lie listening to the house.
scene W: {N} has kept every promise of the partnership: the bills, the birthdays, the hospital visits. This one has slipped, and {N} feels it as a duty left undone.
scene U: {N} lies awake trying to work out when it stopped, and why, as if it were a problem with a solution.
scene B: {N} is still wanted by other people, and knows it. The question is how much longer {N} is willing to wait.
scene R: {N} misses it, plainly and physically, and is tired of pretending not to.
scene G: Everything has its seasons, and the long partnership has been in winter for a while. {N} wonders whether spring is late, or not coming.
- W | set aside one evening a week for the two of you, and keep it | habit | v: tradition, benevolence | self_control: + | chance: 70
- U | ask your partner, gently and honestly, what changed for them | v: self-direction, benevolence | chance: 65
- B | tell them straight what you need, and that things have to change | v: power, self-direction | chance: 55
- R | reach for them tonight, in the dark, without a word | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 60
- G | accept that desire ebbs and flows, and hold them close without asking for more | v: security, benevolence | chance: 70
- W>G | suggest a couples counsellor, and keep every appointment together | door | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 60
- U>W | read up on long relationships, and plan a careful way back to each other | v: benevolence, achievement | chance: 65
- B>U | flirt with someone at the gym, to find out whether you still have it | habit | v: power (face), self-direction | chance: 75
- R>B | start an affair, and stop pretending you can wait | v: hedonism | mark: broke your word | closed: approval: betraying your partner; backfire: found out, and the relationship in crisis | self_control: - | chance: 70
- G>R | take them back to the place where you first fell in love, and see what wakes | v: hedonism, tradition | chance: 60
works: What was stuck begins to move, and {N} sleeps better than in months.
works: Something changes in the house, and {N} feels alive and wanted again.
fails: The subject is raised once, badly, and both of them retreat further.
fails: The silence settles into the shape of the partnership, and {N} lies awake longer.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- with a partner: calls UG (cycle s1)

# gate: age >= 40
== desire and a body that is changing
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 40-85
calls: UG
needs: partner
tone: mixed
life: love, body
horizon: months
roles: partner, a doctor
earth: desire is still there, but the body has changed (the change of life, pills that dull everything, an operation) and no longer answers the way it did
times: Most people from midlife, more than once as the body changes; about half of men aged 40 to 70 report some erection trouble (Massachusetts Male Aging Study, Feldman 1994)
gap: 4-8
scene: {N} still wants {partner}, but the body has changed: the change of life, the pills for blood pressure, the scar from the operation. Last night ended in an embarrassed silence.
scene W: {N} and {partner} promised each other in sickness and in health. This, {N} supposes, is the sickness part, and it deserves to be handled properly.
scene U: {N} reads the small print in the pill packet twice, then the medical websites, then the forums at two in the morning.
scene B: {N} is not ready to give this up. There must be a doctor, a pill or a treatment that will bring it back.
scene R: {N} feels as hungry as at twenty, and the body keeps letting {N} down. It is maddening.
scene G: The old pear tree in the garden still flowers every spring, later and smaller than it used to. {N} watches it and thinks about bodies.
- W | see the doctor, and tell them everything, however embarrassing | v: security, conformity | chance: 80
- U | read everything about it, and work out what might help | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | order the pills online, without a prescription | v: hedonism | mark: broke the law | closed: law: prescription medicine bought without one; backfire: a bad reaction, and a frightening night in hospital | death_if_fails: 0.001 | tech: internet | law: prescription medicines | chance: 75
- R | laugh about it together in bed, and keep trying | v: hedonism, benevolence | self_control: + | chance: 70
- G | let intimacy grow slower and gentler, the way the years want it | v: security, benevolence | chance: 75
- W>U | go to the appointment together, as a couple, and ask every question | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 65
- U>B | find someone online who wants the same, and keep it from your partner | v: hedonism | mark: broke your word | closed: approval: betraying your partner; backfire: found out at the worst moment | self_control: - | tech: online dating | chance: 70
- B>R | stop the pills that dull it, without telling the doctor | v: hedonism | chance: 70
- R>G | tell them every day, in words and touch, how much you still want them | v: benevolence | chance: 75
- G>W | make peace with a partnership of company rather than passion | v: security, tradition | chance: 70
works: The doctor, or the laughter, or the patience helps, and {N} and {partner} find their way back to each other.
works: What comes back is different from before, slower and kinder, and {N} would not trade it.
fails: The embarrassment hardens into avoidance, and they stop touching altogether.
fails: Nothing that is tried works, and for a while {N} feels older than {Ns} years.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- with a partner: calls BR (cycle s2)

