- B>G | sell the big house and move with them to a cottage by the sea | binds | v: security, universalism (nature) | mark: moved away | chance: 75
- R>W | make each other vows on a whim on the beach, with two strangers as witnesses | identity | binds | v: tradition, stimulation | chance: 70
- G>U | walk the old paths together every morning, saying everything you never said | habit | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 75
works: The late season lasts, and {N} and {partner} are the happiest people on the street.
works: The family rolls its eyes, and {N} and {partner} could not care less.
fails: A fall, a cold, an ache, and the late season ends sooner than either of them wanted.
