# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: an invitation for three (pairs D1a)

# gate: age >= 18; the couple: the game draws {friend} and {prospect} so that at least one is of a sex the character is drawn to (any attr)
== an invitation for three
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-55
per_year: 0 0 .015 .008 .003 0
drivers: ties+.4 community-.3 era+.2 unrest-.2
gap: 3-10
excludes: partner
times: estimate: in one US national sample about 18 in 100 men and 10 in 100 women had ever had sex with two others at once (Herbenick and colleagues 2017), most often in their twenties and early thirties, and far more people imagine it than are ever asked (Lehmiller 2018); per single person about 1.5 in 100 a year in the young adult years, under 1 in 100 in the adult years and fewer in midlife are asked by two people they like; never or once in most lives, rarely more
likelier: a wide circle of friends, a city, a permissive era and place, festivals and travel, friends who are an open couple
rarer: a strict faith or family, a small town where everyone talks, few friends, shyness, unrest
tone: mixed
life: love, friends
horizon: moment
roles: friend, prospect
earth: after dinner at their flat, two friends of yours, a couple you have liked for a long time, ask whether you would like to stay the night with them both
scene: After a long dinner at their flat, {friend} and {prospect}, a couple {N} has liked for a long time, look at each other, and then ask {N}, laughing a little, whether {N} would like to stay the night with them both.
scene W: {N} is fond of them both, and of what the two of them have. Whatever happens tonight, {N} does not want to be the thing that breaks it.
scene U: {N} has wondered about this privately more than once. Now the question is real, and there is a great deal to think about.
scene B: Two people who want {N} at the same time. {N} feels the pleasant weight of being the one who decides.
scene R: The wine, the candles, the two of them grinning across the table: {Ns} heart is pounding, and every part of {N} says yes.
scene G: There is so much warmth in the room, between the three of them, and {N} lets the feeling be what it is before thinking at all.
- W | say no, and warn the friends you share what the two of them are like | v: conformity, security | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: spreading their private life; backfire: the friends side with the couple, and the gossip turns round | chance: 60
- U | ask for a week to think, and talk it over with them both first | v: self-direction | chance: 65
- B | say yes, on the condition that you can leave whenever you like | v: power, hedonism | chance: 80
- R | say yes to the three of you, there and then | door | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 78
- G | stay, and let the warmth of the evening decide | v: hedonism, benevolence | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 68
- BG | stay, and keep the night a secret from every friend you share | v: security, hedonism | chance: 75
- BR | say yes, and set out to win one of them away from the other | v: power, hedonism | mark: made an enemy | chance: 45
- UG | say not tonight, and let it grow slowly, if it is going to | v: self-direction, security | chance: 70
- WR | say yes, with one rule agreed at the table: anyone can stop at any time | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 80
- WU | thank them warmly, say no, and talk it through so the friendship holds | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 80
works: The night is warm and kind, and the three of them laugh about it over breakfast.
works: Whatever {N} answers, the friendship with {friend} and {prospect} is still easy a month later.
fails: The morning after is awkward, and the couple stop calling.
fails: Something said that night starts a row between the two of them, and {N} is caught in the middle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a holiday romance (pairs D1b)

# gate: age >= 18
== a holiday romance
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 .04 .025 .012 .006
drivers: money+.5 prosper+.2 health+.2 unrest-.4 ties+.1
gap: 2-6
excludes: partner
times: estimate: a holiday fling is common among young single travellers (surveys of young holidaymakers in resort towns find a large share meeting a new partner abroad, Bellis and colleagues 2004) and rarer later in life; per single person about 4 in 100 a year in the young adult years, 2.5 in the adult years, about 1 in midlife and under 1 after sixty; perhaps a third of people have one at some point (estimate)
likelier: money for travel, youth, a long trip or a summer job abroad, travelling alone or with friends, a recent breakup
rarer: little money, poor health, caring duties, unrest or closed borders, a strict faith or family
tone: joy
life: love, travel
horizon: week
roles: prospect, friend
earth: a week in a town by the sea, far from home, and someone you meet on the second day makes every hour count
scene: On the second day of the holiday, in a café by the harbour, {N} meets {prospect}, and by the fourth day neither of them is pretending to look at the sea.
scene W: {N} came here to rest and be sensible, and has a return ticket for Saturday. {prospect} is not part of any plan.
scene U: {prospect} speaks another language, eats strange breakfasts and knows every alley of the old town. {N} wants to learn all of it.
scene B: {N} has a week of freedom, nobody watching and nothing to lose, and means to make the most of it.
scene R: The sun, the salt, the late nights, and {prospect} laughing on the harbour wall: {N} is in love by Tuesday.
scene G: {N} has fallen into the rhythm of the place: long lunches, a swim at dusk, and {prospect} close by as if it had always been so.
- W | enjoy every day of it, and say a proper goodbye at the bus on Saturday | v: hedonism, conformity | chance: 85
- U | learn their language and their town, and keep writing once you are home | door | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | enjoy the week, and give them a false number on the last morning | v: hedonism, power | chance: 80
- R | ride on the back of their scooter along the cliff road, no helmet | body: light | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | closed: law: riding without a helmet; backfire: a fine, or a fall | death_if_fails: 0.002 | chance: 68
- G | swim out with them to the rocks at night, the way the locals do | door | body: heavy | v: stimulation, universalism (nature) | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: night swimming where the signs forbid it; backfire: a rescue boat, and a fine | death_if_fails: 0.002 | chance: 75
- RG | change your ticket, and stay on with them for another month | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 70
- UB | find out what their life at home is really like before going any deeper | v: security | chance: 75
- UR | write them a long letter on the last night, saying everything | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 80
- WB | invite them to visit your home town, and pay for the ticket and the visa | v: benevolence, security | closed: law: a visa that may be refused; backfire: turned back at the border, and the money gone | chance: 50
- WG | introduce them to your family on a video call on the last night | v: tradition, benevolence | tech: video calls | chance: 65
works: The week is golden from end to end, and {N} goes home brown and happy, with a story for life.
works: {N} and {prospect} keep writing long after the holiday, and the summer lives on.
fails: On the last night {prospect} mentions someone waiting at home, and the week turns sour.
fails: The goodbye is harder than {N} expected, and home looks grey for weeks.
